operates as an online travel company in the United States and internationally. The company operates through B2C, B2B, and trivago segments. The B2C segment includes Brand Expedia, a full-service online travel brand offers various travel products and services; Hotels.com for lodging accommodations; Vrbo, an online marketplace for the alternative accommodations; and Orbitz, Travelocity, ebookers, and Wotif Group. The B2B segment provides various travel and non-travel companies including airlines, offline travel agents, online retailers, corporate travel management, and financial institutions who leverage its travel technology and tap into its diverse supply to augment their offerings and market Expedia Group rates and availabilities to its travelers. The trivago segment sends referrals to online travel companies and travel service providers from hotel metasearch websites. In addition, it provides brand advertising through online and offline channels, loyalty programs, mobile apps, and search engine marketing, as well as metasearch, social media, direct and personalized traveler communications on its websites, and through direct e-mail communication with its travelers. The company was formerly known as Expedia, Inc. and changed its name to Expedia Group, Inc. in March 2018. Expedia Group, Inc. was founded in 1996 and is headquartered in Seattle, Washington.","ceo_bio":"Ms. Ariane  Gorin | CEO & Director | Age 51 | Compensation: $1.9M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 16K people. Revenue per employee of $921K ranks in the top quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers, with revenue growing 10%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $194K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $25K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["Expedia Group, Inc. is a large-cap consumer cyclical business with a $27.9B market cap on $14.7B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +8% over the past three years and +8% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 18% against a 10% cost of capital, a 7-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $3.1B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 21 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 3.00\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.2\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 6.3\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 7.6% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 1.6\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.5) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 7.8% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $3.2M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-3220991.53},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Consumer Cyclical tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Consumer staples outperforming discretionary, signaling cautious spending","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"High market volatility with VIX at 36, signaling elevated fear","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Widening credit spreads suggest growing stress in corporate debt markets","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 39% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Consumer Cyclical sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 5% over 3 months"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Why Expedia (EXPE) is a Top Growth Stock for the Long-Term","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3032447/why-expedia-expe-is-a-top-growth-stock-for-the-long-term?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Czacks_education_growth_score-3032447","date":"2026-11-19","timestamp":1795095903.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.527,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Will Raised Revenue Guidance Change Expedia's (EXPE) Narrative","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/raised-revenue-guidance-change-expedias-232429617.html","date":"2026-11-18","timestamp":1795044269.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.382,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance"]},{"title":"Why (EXPE) Price Action Is Critical for Tactical Trading","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/141/Why_EXPE_Price_Action_Is_Critical_for_Tactical_Trading_111826051602_1795040162.html","date":"2026-11-18","timestamp":1795040162.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.557,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"The Expedia breach s